A slot is a place where another template supplies content.

[codeblock, $code "moth":
    card = [:
        <h1>[$slot title = "Untitled"]</h1>
        <section>[$slot]</section>
    ]

    [card:
        [$in title:Welcome]
        This is the card body.
    ]
]

The named `title` slot receives `Welcome`.

The default slot receives the body text.

Without an insert, `title` shows its `Untitled` default while an empty default
slot renders nothing. Each slot occurrence owns its own compile-time `String`
default, and an explicitly empty insert still suppresses it.

Positional slots use `$slot 1` and are filled by loose head contributions. `$in`
targets a named slot only and has no positional form. Slots that receive no
content and have no default become empty strings.

See @../templates/#template-slots (Template slots) for declaration forms,
positional routing, stored inserts and runtime contributions.
